2196:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp **** OUTPUT PARAMETERS
2197:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp ****     KDT     -   KD-tree
2198:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp **** 
2199:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp **** NOTES
2200:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp **** 
2201:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp **** 1. KD-tree  creation  have O(N*logN) complexity and O(N*(2*NX+NY))  memory
2202:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp ****    requirements.
2203:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp **** 2. Although KD-trees may be used with any combination of N  and  NX,  they
2204:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp ****    are more efficient than brute-force search only when N >> 4^NX. So they
2205:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp ****    are most useful in low-dimensional tasks (NX=2, NX=3). NX=1  is another
2206:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp ****    inefficient case, because  simple  binary  search  (without  additional
2207:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp ****    structures) is much more efficient in such tasks than KD-trees.
