6248:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp **** 1. KD-tree  creation  have O(N*logN) complexity and O(N*(2*NX+NY))  memory
6249:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp ****    requirements.
6250:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp **** 2. Although KD-trees may be used with any combination of N  and  NX,  they
6251:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp ****    are more efficient than brute-force search only when N >> 4^NX. So they
6252:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp ****    are most useful in low-dimensional tasks (NX=2, NX=3). NX=1  is another
6253:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp ****    inefficient case, because  simple  binary  search  (without  additional
6254:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp ****    structures) is much more efficient in such tasks than KD-trees.
