7214:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp ****    be overwritten; trailing part will be left unchanged. So  if  on  input
7215:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp ****    XY = [[A,B],[C,D]], and result is [1,2],  then  on  exit  we  will  get
7216:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp ****    XY = [[1,2],[C,D]]. This is done purposely to increase performance;  if
7217:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp ****    you want function  to  resize  array  according  to  result  size,  use
7218:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp ****    function with same name and suffix 'I'.
7219:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp **** 
