7352:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp **** Tags from last query associated with kdtreerequestbuffer object.
7353:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp **** 
7354:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp **** This function retuns results stored in  the  internal  buffer  of  kd-tree
7355:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp **** object. If you performed buffered requests (ones which  use  instances  of
7356:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp **** kdtreerequestbuffer class), you  should  call  buffered  version  of  this
7357:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp **** function - KDTreeTsqueryresultstags().
7358:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp **** 
7359:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp **** INPUT PARAMETERS
7360:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp ****     KDT     -   KD-tree
7361:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp ****     Buf     -   request  buffer  object  created   for   this   particular
7362:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp ****                 instance of kd-tree structure.
7363:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp ****     Tags    -   possibly pre-allocated buffer. If X is too small to store
7364:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp ****                 result, it is resized. If size(X) is enough to store
7365:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp ****                 result, it is left unchanged.
7366:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp **** 
7367:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp **** OUTPUT PARAMETERS
7368:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp ****     Tags    -   filled with tags associated with points,
7369:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp ****                 or, when no tags were supplied, with zeros
7370:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp **** 
7371:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp **** NOTES
7372:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp **** 1. points are ordered by distance from the query point (first = closest)
7373:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp **** 2. if  XY is larger than required to store result, only leading part  will
7374:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp ****    be overwritten; trailing part will be left unchanged. So  if  on  input
7375:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp ****    XY = [[A,B],[C,D]], and result is [1,2],  then  on  exit  we  will  get
7376:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp ****    XY = [[1,2],[C,D]]. This is done purposely to increase performance;  if
7377:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp ****    you want function  to  resize  array  according  to  result  size,  use
7378:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp ****    function with same name and suffix 'I'.
7379:libs/alglib/src/alglibmisc.cpp **** 
